@startuml gate-workflow
' The gate loop: run, resolve, re-check. Traced against
' src/afriend/commands/run.py (cmd_run's gate branch),
' commands/resolve.py, and resolutions.py.

' Theme: colours sampled from docs/images/brand/afriend-logo-512.png.
' Avenir Next and SF Mono ship with macOS and are absent from the CI runner,
' which only checks that a source renders -- the committed PNG and SVG pair
' is produced by `make diagrams` on a machine that has them.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName "Avenir Next"
skinparam defaultMonospacedFontName "SF Mono"
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #6E8288
skinparam ArrowFontColor #5B7079
skinparam ArrowFontSize 12
skinparam TitleFontSize 19
skinparam TitleFontColor #2D424E
skinparam legendBackgroundColor #F8FCFC
skinparam legendBorderColor #A8C3CC
skinparam legendFontSize 12
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #F4F1E8
skinparam noteBorderColor #B3AA97
skinparam noteFontColor #4A4436
skinparam noteFontSize 12
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #7E99A3
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #EAF3F4
skinparam ActivityFontColor #2D424E
skinparam ActivityBorderThickness 1
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #E7F9F8
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #4F7981
skinparam ActivityDiamondFontColor #2D424E
skinparam ActivityDiamondFontSize 12
skinparam PartitionBorderColor #A8C3CC
skinparam PartitionBackgroundColor #F8FCFC
skinparam PartitionFontColor #4F7981

' Semantic fills are <style> classes, not the `#RRGGBB:label;` prefix --
' From 1.2026.7, an inline-coloured activity directly before an `if`, at a
' group boundary, or ending an `if` branch with an empty or absent `else`
' inside a group fails the whole source ("Cannot find group", "Cannot find
' if", "Cannot find repeat", "Syntax Error?"). One property per line:
' `{ BackgroundColor #A  LineColor #B }`
' parses as a single malformed value and the class is dropped in silence,
' leaving the tagged nodes unstyled in a diagram that still "succeeds".
<style>
.downgrade {
  BackgroundColor #F6E7C8
  LineColor #C79B4E
}
.failed {
  BackgroundColor #F3D7D2
  LineColor #C07A6E
}
.success {
  BackgroundColor #D9E8D5
  LineColor #7A9B72
}
.command {
  BackgroundColor #D8EDEC
  LineColor #4F7981
}
</style>

title The gate loop

start

:afriend run spec.md "--mode gate"; <<command>>
:critique, then cross-examine;

if (any non-advisory claim\nnot cleared by its state?) then (no)
  :exit 0 — gate clear; <<success>>
  stop
else (yes)
endif

:exit 1 — names each blocking claim; <<failed>>

note right
  Only settled-refuted clears on its
  own. superseded is exempt because its
  successor carries the question.
  discarded and incomplete both need a
  Resolution: no working assessment is
  not a pass.
end note

repeat
  :a human changes something;
  :afriend resolve RUN_ID\nclaim = c-0001@1\ndisposition = fixed\nevidence = src/auth.py:38; <<command>>

  if (evidence names a location?) then (no)
    :exit 2 — refused; <<failed>>
    stop
  else (yes)
  endif

  :compare that location against\nthe run's frozen copy or snapshot;

  if (fixed, but nothing changed there?) then (yes)
    :exit 2 — refused; <<failed>>
    stop
  else (no)
  endif

  :append resolution\nverified = changed | unchanged | unverifiable;
repeat while (claims still blocking?) is (yes) not (no)

:exit 0 — gate clear; <<success>>
stop

@enduml
